# Filament 4 Admin Conventions

## Resource Structure

Each Resource lives at `app/Filament/Resources/{Name}Resource.php` with sub-folders:

- `Pages/List{Name}.php`
- `Pages/Create{Name}.php`
- `Pages/Edit{Name}.php`
- `Pages/View{Name}.php` (when read-only view is needed)
- `RelationManagers/*RelationManager.php`

## Schema-based Forms (Filament 4)

Use the `Schema::make()` builder syntax. Do NOT use the legacy `Form::make()` API from Filament 3.

```php
public static function form(Schema $schema): Schema
{
    return $schema->components([
        TextInput::make('name')->required()->maxLength(255),
        Select::make('category_id')->relationship('category', 'name')->preload(),
    ]);
}
```

## Bulk Import

Use `Filament\Actions\Importer` for CSV imports. Failed rows are persisted in the `failed_import_rows` table (migration `2026_04_09_005325_create_failed_import_rows_table.php` already exists). Imports MUST run on the queue (`shouldQueue = true`).

Existing importers: `AuthorImporter`, `SupplierImporter`, `BookImporter` — follow the same shape for new ones.

## Relation Managers

For one-to-many / many-to-many relations, register a Relation Manager in the parent Resource's `getRelations()`. Existing patterns: `BooksRelationManager`, `InventoriesRelationManager`, `PromotionItemsRelationManager`.

## Tables

Define searchable, sortable, and filterable columns explicitly. Use `BadgeColumn` for enums. Apply a soft-delete filter (`TrashedFilter`) when the model uses `SoftDeletes`.
